text:
alex: Running the onboarding sample (node, express, retry-mw) — intermittently seeing two different req ids for the same logical request and one of the emits still contains a raw email. Repro + notes below.

sophia: can you paste the minimal log lines + how you initialize the SDK?

alex: sanitized snippet from local run:
```
INFO 2026-09-12T10:01:01Z request_id=rq-100 user=eva@example.com event=auth.start
INFO 2026-09-12T10:01:02Z request_id=rq-100 event=auth.retry attempt=1
WARN 2026-09-12T10:01:03Z request_id=rq-200 user=eva@example.com event=auth.finish
```
sdk init in sampleapp:
```js
Telemetry.init({ hooks: [attachOtelHook, redactHook, sampleHook] })
```
I suspect retry-mw is re-dispatching the handler and creating a new span/context so an attach-time redact misses the final emit.

dan: interesting — do you also see a change in the trace headers? like traceparent or x-request-id being replaced by the retry path?

alex: yes — traceparent on the final emit shows a new trace; the retry code doesn't preserve the incoming x-request-id on re-dispatch.

sophia: smells like two related issues: (1) request fingerprinting / header preservation in middleware, and (2) redact hook timing (attach vs emit). If attach-only, re-emits bypass it.

logger-bot: created ticket DE-7001: "node sampleapp: retry re-dispatch causes req_id drift + missed PII redaction" — https://jira/redwood/DE-7001 :rotating_light:

carol: i ran a quick experiment — moving redaction to the final emit pipeline fixed the leak locally. Patch in sampleapp:
```js
// sampleapp quickfix
logger.on('record', (rec) => {
  if (!rec.__pii_redacted) { redactPII(rec); rec.__pii_redacted = true }
});
```
works, but we need to think about perf and correctness at SDK level.

dan: two prongs for a robust fix: (A) make SDK do emit-time redaction by default (with an opt-in attach-mode for legacy customers), and (B) add a middleware helper that preserves the inbound request id / trace headers when re-dispatching. Also consider a stable request_fingerprint header to correlate across replays.

sophia: agree. additional mitigations: add a fastpath classifier so redact can cheaply skip records without PII (cheap regex or metadata check) and keep a _redacted marker to avoid double work.

alex: i sketched a small SDK change that is backwards-compatible:
```js
// pseudocode in SDK default pipeline
function onEmit(rec) {
  if (rec.__pii_redacted) return;
  if (looksLikePII(rec)) { redactPII(rec) }
  rec.__pii_redacted = true;
  out.emit(rec);
}
// old behavior still available via Telemetry.init({ redactMode: 'attach' })
```

carol: also recommend instrumenting CI to fail if any log output in integration tests contains an email regex. That gives us a safety net while we ship.

dan: good call. add an integration test that exercises express retry-mw re-dispatch: assert logs.map(l => l.request_id) are stable (or match a preserved x-request-id header) and assert no raw emails. Sketch:
```js
await runHarnessWithRetryReplay();
expect(logs.map(l => l.request_id).filter(Boolean)).toEqual(['rq-100']);
expect(logs.join('')).not.toMatch(/[\w.-]+@[\w.-]+/);
```

sophia: runtime notes: node's async_hooks and certain runtimes (bun) can affect context propagation. Keep this fix scoped to SDK's log pipeline and add a separate follow-up to audit async context propagation across runtimes.

alex: plan summary: (1) add integration test for retry-replay path (carol + dan), (2) implement SDK emit-time redact with cheap looksLikePII fastpath + __pii_redacted marker (sophia will own PR), (3) provide middleware helper to preserve inbound x-request-id / traceparent when re-dispatching (dan to draft), (4) CI rule to fail on raw-email in integration logs, (5) ship 0.12.4-canary and monitor PII alerts.

logger-bot: linked DE-7001 to components: SDK/Node, Telemetry, DevEx-tests.

sophia: i'll open the canary PR and include microbench numbers for emit vs attach redaction. dan, can you include a small note in the migration guide about the new default and how to opt back?

dan: yep. also will add a tiny middleware snippet to the sampleapp that preserves headers:```js
function preserveId(req, next) {
  const id = req.headers['x-request-id'] || genId();
  req.headers['x-request-id'] = id;
  return next();
}
```

carol: i'll add the test harness and CI assertion. leaving DE-7001 with checklist and assigning owners. thanks all :thumbsup:
